The '''Suzuki SV650''' and its variants are street motorcycles manufactured since 1999 by [[Suzuki]]. In 2009, Suzuki replaced the standard SV650 with the [[Suzuki SFV650 Gladius|SFV650 Gladius]]. In 2016, the Gladius name was discontinued and the 2017 model was reverted to SV650.

Other twin cylinder motorcycles in the class include the [[Yamaha MT-07|Yamaha MT07]] / [[Yamaha XSR700]] and [[Kawasaki Z series|Kawasaki Z650]] / [[Kawasaki Ninja|Kawasaki Ninja 650]].  The SV650 is more affordable than the likes of the [[Ducati Monster]], [[Ducati Scrambler (2015)|Ducati Scrambler]], and [[KTM 790 Duke]], but has similar performance.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.bikeme.tv/index.php/2017-suzuki-sv650-lam-sweet-neat/ |author=Ben Akhurst |title=2017 Suzuki SV650 LAM – SWEET & NEAT |work=BIKE ME! |date=2016-06-14 |access-date=2016-07-24}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.revzilla.com/common-tread/is-the-600-cc-race-replica-doomed |author=Mark Gardiner |title=Is the 600 cc race replica doomed to extinction? |work=[[RevZilla.com|RevZilla]] |date=2016-06-30 |access-date=2016-07-24}}</ref>

